/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/bacondecomp/doc/bacon.Rmd:57:  aes(x = weight, y = estimate, shape = factor(type)) +
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/bacondecomp/doc/bacon.Rmd:62:In this example, one estimate has almost 60 percent of the weight: states treated in 2006 vs states that are never treated.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/bacondecomp/doc/bacon.Rmd:66:* When including controls there is an additional source of identifying variation that comes from within treatment timing group. It is noted as $\hat{\beta^p_w}$. $\Omega$ is the weight given to this estimate in the two-way fixed effects estimate. 
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/bacondecomp/doc/bacon.Rmd:68:* The 2x2s are no longer decomposed into "early vs late" and "late vs early" estimates. For each treatment group dyad, there is only one estimate, $\hat{\beta}^d_{b, k, l}$ which gets weight $s_{k, l}$.
